%I A401328 #15 Oct 20 2026 22:20:20
%S A401328 1,1,1,2,1,1,4,3,1,1,4,4,2,1,1,6,5,4,3,1,1,6,6,4,3,2,1,1,8,7,6,4,3,3,
%T A401328 1,1,9,8,7,6,4,4,2,1,1,10,9,8,7,6,5,4,3,1,1,10,10,9,8,6,5,4,4,2,1,1,
%U A401328 12,11,10,9,8,6,5,5,4,3,1,1,12,12,10,9,8,7,5,5,4,3,2,1,1
%N A401328 Square array A(n,k), n >= 0, k >= 1, read by antidiagonals downwards, where A(n,k) is the number of distinct values of s_k(n+1), ..., s_k(n+k), and s_k(m) is the largest divisor of m with all prime factors less than k.
%H A401328 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A401328/b401328.txt">Antidiagonals n = 0..139, flattened</a>
%H A401328 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/461">Erdős Problem 461</a>, Erdős Problems.
%e A401328 Square array begins:
%e A401328   1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 6, 6, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 6, 7, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 3, 3, 4, 6, 7, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 6, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 5, 6, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 5, 5, ...
%e A401328   1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 5, 6, ...
%e A401328   ...
%o A401328 (PARI) s(n, k) = my(r=1); forprime(p=2, k-1, r*=p^valuation(n, p)); r;
%o A401328 a(n, k) = #Set(vector(k, j, s(n+j,k)));
%K A401328 nonn,tabl,new
%O A401328 0,4
%A A401328 _Seiichi Manyama_, Oct 20 2026
